cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization in your research, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Axiomatic & Constructive Quantum Field Theory in Lean 4"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "P3r0o0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/P3r0o0/Axiomatic-Constructive-Quantum-Field-Theory-in-Lean-4"
url: "https://github.com/P3r0o0/Axiomatic-Constructive-Quantum-Field-Theory-in-Lean-4"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-11-21"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 formalization of 4-dimensional relativistic axiomatic
  and constructive Quantum Field Theory built on Mathlib (v4.32.2), covering
  complex Lorentz geometry and Jost's theorem, UV-cutoff-free cone Vladimirov
  boundary values, general n-dimensional Malgrange-Zerner and distributional
  Edge-of-the-Wedge theorems, general-spin Bargmann-Hall-Wightman continuation,
  PCT and unconditional Spin-Statistics theorems, pure-Euclidean all n-point
  Osterwalder-Schrader reconstruction, relativistic Haag-Ruelle scattering
  theory, and constructive 4D massive neutral/charged Klein-Gordon and
  Majorana/charged spin-1/2 Dirac models.
keywords:
  - "Lean 4"
  - "Mathlib"
  - "quantum field theory"
  - "axiomatic quantum field theory"
  - "constructive quantum field theory"
  - "Wightman axioms"
  - "Osterwalder-Schrader reconstruction"
  - "Spin-Statistics theorem"
  - "PCT theorem"
  - "Haag-Ruelle scattering"
  - "formalized mathematics"
